  {
    "id": "10_approx_ratio_intro",
    "narration": "The approximation ratio is the heart of these algorithms. For minimization problems, it's the ratio of the algorithm's solution cost to the optimal cost. For maximization, it's the optimal value divided by the algorithm's value. A 2-approximation for vertex cover, for instance, means our solution is guaranteed to be at most twice as large as the best possible.",
