  },
  {
    "id": "14_preset_path_graph",
    "narration": "Consider a simple path graph with five vertices in a line. The goal is to select as few vertices as possible so that every edge is covered. This structure is easy to visualize and helps us understand how the approximation algorithm operates step by step.",
