    "narration": "Now let's build the recursion tree one level at a time to see its geometry directly. Starting from the root representing the full problem of size 16, each step adds exactly one node — first size 8, then 4, then 2. Because a equals 1, there is never a moment of branching: the tree grows straight downward as a single vertical chain. This chain structure is the geometric reason Binary Search is logarithmic — its depth, log base 2 of n, directly equals the total number of comparisons in the worst case.",
    "focusTarget": "#treeSVG"
